PS5 display on 7.3.1 + rmux shitshow: what his HDMI rework doesn't have

- Re-arm (PR #46): the same display re-announcing wipes the bridge output; re-arm unless the picture comes up
  (Verde 0x03, FLAVA3 0x04). Uses rmux's "same" (EDID and FRL rate).
- Session switch: a hotplug only for a new or different display (a same-display hotplug made the next compositor
  re-announce in a loop); the console re-arm waits rearm_quiet_ms after a mode setup
- FLAVA3: no "back to unplugged / wait resolution" event sequences (black screen at boot on some TVs)
- EDID keep: an invalid or short announcement keeps the previous EDID (else "generic display", 1080p only)
- EDID fallback: every DisplayPort connector gets the EDID when none is bound
- SCDC: Source Version at every setup (TVs exposing their HDMI 2.x EDID only then, issue #11), TMDS_Config for
  every SCDC sink (TVs falling back to HDMI 1.4)
- Sleep: muted and out of HDR while the output is down (TVs flickering between HDR and no signal)
- Full-rate DP link to the HDMI bridge (it fails to sync on lower rates)
- Verde: IT content and content type "game" in the AVI InfoFrame
- VRR on FLAVA3 (hsgodd, Lawson): follow block, stock PHY tail and VSync block, never below 48 Hz, HDMI VRR displays
  only, open-ended VRRmax and HF-SCDB; hdmi.vrr, hdmi.icc_trace, hdmi.vrr_measure
